    "Checkout locks and the lane registry: which session works in which checkout, on which branch, on which units.\n"
    "\n"
    "    lane_lock claim   [--checkout PATH] [--branch B] [--units u1,u2] [--session ID] [--pid N] [--note TEXT] [--force]\n"
    "    lane_lock release [--checkout PATH] [--session ID] | --all | --stale | --id ID\n"
    "    lane_lock status\n"
    "    lane_lock check   [--checkout PATH] [--units u1,u2] [--session ID] [--hook]\n"
    "\n"
    "A claim is one JSON file in <git common dir>/lane-locks/ (shared by every worktree of the repository, never\n"
    "versioned): session, checkout, branch, units, pid, host, time and heartbeat. One claim per session and checkout;\n"
    "claiming again updates it (the fields given replace the old ones) and refreshes the heartbeat.\n"
    "\n"
    "  claim    records the claim; refuses (exit 1) when another session's live claim holds the same checkout or one of\n"
    "           the units, unless --force. --checkout defaults to the checkout of the working directory, --branch to\n"
    "           its current branch.\n"
    "  release  removes this session's claim of the checkout (--all: every claim of this session; --stale: every stale\n"
    "           claim, any session; --id: one claim by its id, as status prints it).\n"
    "  status   every claim: live or stale, age, and the checkout's current branch when it is not the claimed one.\n"
    "  check    exit 0 when nothing conflicts, else exit 1 with one line per conflict: another session's live claim of\n"
    "           the checkout or of an overlapping unit, or this session's own claim of the checkout whose branch is not\n"
    "           the one checked out (the checkout was switched under it). Refreshes this session's own claim. Stale\n"
    "           claims are reported, never block. --hook (for a post-checkout hook): warn only, always exit 0.\n"
    "\n"
    "The session is --session, else $LANE_SESSION, else $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, else user@host. The pid is --pid,\n"
    "else $CLAUDE_PID (the session's own long-lived process), else none. A claim is stale when its pid is dead (same\n"
    "host) or its heartbeat is older than --ttl hours (default 12).\n"
    "\n"
    "A tool that writes into a checkout (a merge or batch driver) calls dk_lane_check() before it writes.\n"
